§§ `s 10(1) a cash grant that should not have been paid`
-- inputs: disbursed as a cash grant, recipient is an eligible individual, recipient is eligible for that cash grant, amount paid, amount the recipient is eligible to receive
-- (the amounts below are stand-ins)
-- not a cash grant: nothing is made recoverable by s 10(1)
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) 100 (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 0
-- (a)(i): the recipient is not an eligible individual -- the whole amount paid
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING 100 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 100
-- (a)(i) not known
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) 100 (JUST 50) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a)(ii): an eligible individual not eligible for that cash grant -- the whole amount paid
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) 100 (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 100
-- (a)(ii) not known
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING 100 (JUST 50) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b): paid more than the recipient is eligible to receive -- the excess
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 100 (JUST 60) EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 101 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 1
-- (b): paid the amount eligible, or less -- nothing is recoverable
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 100 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 99 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 0
-- (b): the amount the recipient is eligible to receive is not known
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 100 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Added 2026-11-04 after the independent pass.  Status as an eligible individual not known, but known not eligible for that cash grant:
-- if the recipient is not an eligible individual, (a)(i) ("is not an eligible individual") makes the amount paid recoverable;
-- if the recipient is an eligible individual, (a)(ii) ("is an eligible individual, but is not eligible for that cash grant") does;
-- so the whole amount paid is recoverable either way, and the unknown status does not matter.
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) 1000 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 1000
-- the same when the amount the recipient is eligible to receive is known: limb (a) gives the whole 1000, not the 200 of limb (b)
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) 1000 (JUST 800) EQUALS JUST 1000
-- both known: (a)(i) and (a)(ii) are each met or not as stated, the whole amount paid
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) 1000 (JUST 800) EQUALS JUST 1000
-- Status not known and entitlement to that cash grant not known either: limb (a) would give the whole 1000 and limb (b) would give 200,
-- and the text says only "the amount paid or paid in excess (as the case may be)", so which applies cannot be told from the text: NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE NOTHING NOTHING 1000 (JUST 800) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE NOTHING NOTHING 1000 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Status not known, known eligible for that cash grant: (a)(i) would give 1000 and (b) would give 200: NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) 1000 (JUST 800) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a cash grant: nothing is made recoverable by this subsection, whatever else is unknown
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` FALSE NOTHING NOTHING 1000 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 0

§§ `s 10(2) a benefit obtained by a false statement or document`
-- inputs: obtained by a false or misleading statement made knowingly or recklessly, obtained by a document known or ought to be known to be false, amount so obtained (a stand-in)
#ASSERT `s 10(2) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE FALSE 100 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 10(2) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` FALSE TRUE 100 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 10(2) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` TRUE TRUE 100 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 10(2) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` FALSE FALSE 100 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 10(3) recovery by set-off or otherwise`
-- inputs: the person recovering is an administrator, an amount is due under s 10(1) or (2), the source
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the administrator may recover the amount from the source` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `a cash grant or other benefit the recipient is eligible to receive under the Scheme` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the administrator may recover the amount from the source` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `another sum payable to the recipient by the administrator` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the administrator may recover the amount from the source` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `another source` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the administrator may recover the amount from the source` (JUST TRUE) FALSE `a cash grant or other benefit the recipient is eligible to receive under the Scheme` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the administrator may recover the amount from the source` (JUST FALSE) TRUE `a cash grant or other benefit the recipient is eligible to receive under the Scheme` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(3) the administrator may recover the amount from the source` NOTHING TRUE `a cash grant or other benefit the recipient is eligible to receive under the Scheme` EQUALS NOTHING
